  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nIssued 331 AM MDT SUN JUL 26 2026\nA strong high pressure system sitting off the four corners \nregion, and a trough over British Columbia, will keep our area \nunder southwesterly flow aloft. Monsoonal moisture will remain \nsouth and east of our area in this pattern, leading to a hot, \ndry, and breezy long-term period. Near (leaning above) normal \ntemperatures will warm to around 5 degrees above normal come \nThursday, as the aforementioned high pressure system shifts west\nover the Great basin. Sunday may see a cooldown to near-normal \ntemperatures, depending on how far down troughing from the \nnorthwest coast reaches into our area.",
